$ A-B gap eutectic
$ Written by phase-diagram-explorer 0.2.0.
$ Synthetic test fixture: tests/fixtures/gap_eutectic.json exported with write_tdb.
$ Source: Synthetic system for validating invariant detection with composition
$ sets: the regular solution ALPHA (L0 = 20000 J/mol, Tc = 1202.73 K) plus an
$ ideal LIQUID whose end members both melt at 1000 K (dHfus = 10000 J/mol).
$ Below the liquidus minimum the liquid decomposes eutectically into the two
$ composition sets of ALPHA, symmetrically about x = 0.5.
$
ELEMENT /-   ELECTRON_GAS  0.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT VA   VACUUM        0.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT A ALPHA 50.0 0.0 0.0 !
ELEMENT B ALPHA 100.0 0.0 0.0 !

TYPE_DEFINITION % SEQ * !
DEFINE_SYSTEM_DEFAULT ELEMENT 2 !
DEFAULT_COMMAND DEF_SYS_ELEMENT VA /- !

PHASE LIQUID % 1 1.0 !
CONSTITUENT LIQUID :A,B: !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,A;0) 1.0 10000.0-10.0*T; 10000.0 N !
PARAMETER G(LIQUID,B;0) 1.0 10000.0-10.0*T; 10000.0 N !

PHASE ALPHA % 1 1.0 !
CONSTITUENT ALPHA :A,B: !
PARAMETER G(ALPHA,A;0) 1.0 0.0; 10000.0 N !
PARAMETER G(ALPHA,B;0) 1.0 0.0; 10000.0 N !
PARAMETER L(ALPHA,A,B;0) 1.0 20000.0; 10000.0 N !
